    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d413">

                <pb facs="0465" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg451"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.01/655a: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Certain Diplomatic Representatives in the American
                            Republics
                    </hi><anchor n="64" xml:id="d413-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-17T21:00:00-04:00">February 17,
                            1944—9 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For your confidential information the Department is not greatly impressed with
                    the recent changes which have been announced in the Junta at La Paz, namely the
                    inclusion in the Cabinet of Messrs. Pacheco,<anchor n="65" xml:id="d413-f2"/>
                        Otazo<anchor n="66" xml:id="d413-f3"/> and Guevara,<anchor n="67"
                        xml:id="d413-f4"/> and it is not felt that these shifts have materially
                    altered the character of the Junta which we announced on January 24 we did not
                    intend to recognize for the present. The Department would be pleased to receive
                    any pertinent information which you may have in regard to the opinions of the
                    Government to which you are accredited on this matter.</p>
                <p>However, it is not deemed advisable for you to gratuitously offer to the Foreign
                    Minister the information contained in the first paragraph of this telegram but
                    it is for your guidance in case he should approach you on the subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d413-f1" n="64" type="source" xml:id="d413-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Chile, Peru, Paraguay, Mexico, Brazil, Cuba, Colombia, and Venezuela.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d413-f2" n="65" xml:id="d413-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Alfredo Pacheco, newly designated Minister of Government.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d413-f3" n="66" xml:id="d413-f3-content">
                <p>Rafael Otazo, appointed Minister of Agriculture, February 11, 1944.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d413-f4" n="67" xml:id="d413-f4-content">
                <p>Walter Guevara Arze, Secretary General of the Junta.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
